Now the services. BloodUnitService: inbound + result callback. ReleaseService: release with idempotency.

BloodUnitService:

```java
@Service
public class BloodUnitService {
    private final BloodUnitRepository units;
    private final ResultEventRepository events;
    private final Clock clock;

    @Transactional
    public UnitResponse inbound(InboundRequest req) {
        try {
            units.insert(req.barcode(), req.expiryDate(), Instant.now(clock));
        } catch (DuplicateKeyException e) {
            throw new ConflictException("DUPLICATE_BARCODE", ..., null);
        }
        return toResponse(units.findByBarcode(req.barcode()).orElseThrow());
    }

    @Transactional
    public UnitResponse recordResult(String barcode, ResultCallbackRequest req) {
        BloodUnit unit = units.findByBarcodeForUpdate(barcode)
            .orElseThrow(() -> new NotFoundException("条码不存在: " + barcode));
        Instant now = Instant.now(clock);
        if (unit.status().isTerminal()) {
            events.insert(barcode, req.testType(), req.result(), true, now);
            return toResponse(unit); // 迟到事件，不改变状态
        }
        // apply result
        TestResultValue initial = unit.initialResult();
        TestResultValue recheck = unit.recheckResult();
        if (req.testType() == INITIAL) initial = req.result(); else recheck = req.result();
        UnitStatus newStatus = decide(initial, recheck);
        BloodUnit updated = new BloodUnit(..., initial, recheck, ..., newStatus...);
        units.updateResultsAndStatus(updated, now);
        events.insert(barcode, req.testType(), req.result(), false, now);
        return toResponse(...);
    }

    static UnitStatus decide(initial, recheck) {
        if (initial == FAIL || recheck == FAIL) return DISCARDED;
        if (initial == PASS && recheck == PASS) return RELEASABLE;
        if (initial == null && recheck == null) return PENDING_TEST;
        return QUARANTINED;
    }
}
```

Wait: if one is null and other is PASS → QUARANTINED. If one null and other FAIL → DISCARDED (covered). Duplicate same result re-callback: e.g. INITIAL PASS arrives twice — second time, status not terminal, sets initial=PASS again, same state; event recorded as non-late. Fine (idempotent-ish).

ReleaseService:

```java
@Service
public class ReleaseService {
    @Transactional
    public ReleaseResponse release(ReleaseRequest req) {
        String fingerprint = fingerprint(req);
        Optional<ReleaseOrder> existing = orders.findByRequestId(req.requestId());
        if (existing.isPresent()) {
            ReleaseOrder order = existing.get();
            if (!order.fingerprint().equals(fingerprint)) {
                throw new ConflictException("IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT", "同键异参", currentStatusOf(order.barcode()));
            }
            // 同键同参：返回首次结果
            UnitStatus status = currentStatusOf(order.barcode());
            return new ReleaseResponse(order.requestId(), order.barcode(), order.outcome(), status, order.detail());
        }
        BloodUnit unit = units.findByBarcodeForUpdate(req.barcode())
            .orElseThrow(() -> new NotFoundException(...));
        Instant now = Instant.now(clock);
        // 过期判定：任何放行请求中过期一律拒绝并标记过期报废
        if (unit.isExpiredAt(now) && unit.status() != RELEASED) {
            if (unit.status() != EXPIRED_DISCARDED && unit.status() != DISCARDED) {
                units.updateStatus(unit, EXPIRED_DISCARDED, now);
            }
            ... record order REJECTED, throw ConflictException("EXPIRED", ..., EXPIRED_DISCARDED)?
        }
        ...
    }
}
```

Hmm — should rejected releases record a release_order row? The idempotency spec: "同键同参返回首次结果". If first request was rejected (e.g. unit quarantined), and the same requestId is replayed later after unit becomes releasable — should it return the first (rejected) result or execute? "同键同参返回首次结果" — return first result. So record REJECTED orders too. But careful: recording rejected order for a NOT_FOUND barcode — then replay would return first result referencing a nonexistent barcode. NotFound case: don't record order (barcode doesn't exist → 404, no order). Reasonable.

Also concurrent same requestId inserts: unique constraint on request_id; second insert fails with DuplicateKeyException → catch, re-query, treat as replay (compare fingerprint). Need to handle: since we insert the order at the end of the transaction, concurrent duplicates would be caught at insert time. But with H2 and row lock on blood_unit, two concurrent releases for the same barcode serialize on the unit row lock. Different requestIds, same barcode: first commits RELEASED; second acquires lock, sees status RELEASED → reject with current status RELEASED. Good — "并发对同一条码放行只允许成功一次，另一请求得到该单位当前真实状态".

For rejected outcomes: do we throw ConflictException or return 200 with REJECTED? Spec: "另一请求得到该单位当前真实状态" — I'll return 409 with ApiError body carrying currentStatus for rejections, EXCEPT... Hmm, but then "同键同参返回首次结果" — if first result was a rejection (409), replay should also return 409 with same info. If first was success (200), replay returns 200 with RELEASED outcome.

Design decision: 
- Success → 200 ReleaseResponse(outcome=RELEASED).
- Rejection → 409 ApiError(code, message, currentStatus). Codes: UNIT_EXPIRED (marks EXPIRED_DISCARDED), UNIT_NOT_RELEASABLE (status quarantined/pending/discarded/released...), IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT.
- Replay of a recorded REJECTED order → 409 with stored detail and current status. Replay of RELEASED order → 200.

But wait — for expired marking: if unit already DISCARDED (terminal, failed test) and also expired — "过期单位在任何放行请求中一律拒绝并标记过期报废，与人工报废口径一致". If already DISCARDED, keep DISCARDED (terminal). Mark EXPIRED_DISCARDED only from non-terminal states (PENDING_TEST, QUARANTINED, RELEASABLE). If RELEASED already — can a release request come for a released unit? Yes, concurrent second request. It's released, not expired-marked (already issued blood). Reject with current status RELEASED. Should expiry check apply to RELEASED units? No — already released before expiry. So expiry check only when status is non-terminal.

Order of checks in release:
1. Lock unit row.
2. If status terminal:
   - RELEASED → reject 409 currentStatus RELEASED ("已放行，不允许重复放行").
   - DISCARDED → reject 409 DISCARDED.
   - EXPIRED_DISCARDED → reject 409 EXPIRED_DISCARDED.
   Record REJECTED order? For replay consistency, yes record. But careful: recording rejected orders for every concurrent attempt — each has unique requestId so fine.
3. If expired at now → updateStatus EXPIRED_DISCARDED, record REJECTED order, throw 409 with EXPIRED_DISCARDED.
4. If status != RELEASABLE → record REJECTED, throw 409 with current status.
5. Else: updateStatus RELEASED, insert issue_record, insert order RELEASED, return 200.

Atomicity: all in one @Transactional. 

Race "复检合格回传 vs 过期判定": both take row lock; serialized. If callback commits first (RELEASABLE), release tx then sees RELEASABLE but expired → EXPIRED_DISCARDED, reject. If release tx first → EXPIRED_DISCARDED; callback sees terminal → late event. Unique terminal state either way. 

DuplicateKeyException on order insert (same requestId concurrently): catch around insert? The insert happens inside transaction; on duplicate key, H2 throws DuplicateKeyException. To handle replay properly, catch it, and... transaction may be marked rollback-only? With Spring, exception thrown → if we catch it inside @Transactional method, transaction isn't automatically rollback-only unless the exception propagates through a transactional proxy. H2 doesn't mark the tx rollback-only at JDBC level. So catch DuplicateKeyException, query existing order, return replay result. That works.

Actually simpler: check-then-act with the unique constraint as backstop, catching DuplicateKeyException → replay path.

Fingerprint: SHA-256 hex of requestId + "|" + barcode + "|" + windowStart + "|" + windowEnd.

Now the "currentStatusOf" for idempotency conflict on unknown barcode — barcode may not exist; then currentStatus null.

